  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "title": "Question and scope",
      "body": "This selected original protocol 1.0.0 run evaluates three NQ setups during 20:00–00:00 New York time: A, a confirmed reversal toward prior RTH POC after a VAH/VAL excursion; B, developing Asia value-boundary break and retest; C, a fade at a pre-touch selected HVN. The publication emphasizes validation 2024–2025 with a fixed thirty-minute horizon."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "findings",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "POC reversal contrasts are inconclusive. The short-side value-boundary retest has favorable matched excursion evidence, while the short-side HVN fade has worse adverse excursion. Results differ by setup and side. They remain exploratory descriptive paths; this page does not incorporate the separate D/E extension."
    },
