    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "methods",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "A is a confirmed reversal toward POC after an upper/lower excursion, not a generic value-area reentry rule. B confirms a retest of developing VAH/VAL. C selects its overhead/below HVN before the touch and counts actual range contact, not a gap crossing. Entry references are next one-minute opens; thirty-minute paths remain within the midnight deadline. Volume profiles allocate bar volume uniformly across price bins, an approximation rather than trade-by-trade volume at price. Matched controls share year, side, New York hour and development volatility quintile. Positive MFE differences favor the candidate; positive MAE differences mean more adverse excursion. Saved 95% intervals use two-week moving ISO-week bootstrap blocks. A variable midnight deadline is separate and excluded here."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "Older years have sparse one-minute source coverage; the saved quality rows disclose it. Historical 2010–2019, development 2020–2023, validation 2024–2025 and 2026 YTD are chronological diagnostics, not pristine confirmation. Adjustment mapping and whole-day eligibility are retrospective. Bar-volume profiles, intrabar ordering and live fills lack independent indicator/execution parity. An original event-ledger manifest is absent; saved report, configuration and artifact ledgers still provide bounded presentation provenance."
    },
